                                "sense_id": "fc1dc592-6101-3173-aad9-97d1ce6c3c9e",
                                "text": "He understood that once Cully had slept in freedom for a whole night he would be wild again and irreclaimable. Cully was a passager. But if the poor Wart could only mark him to roost, and if Hob would only arrive then with a dark lantern, they might still take him that night by climbing the tree, while he was sleepy and muddled with the light."
